WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.477
A derived column is a new variable created from existing data.

00:00:04.477 --> 00:00:11.657
In the example, we calculate tax from the amount, then create a total that includes tax.

00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:16.782
We also create an order-size category using numeric ranges.

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:22.107
Pandas is designed to perform these calculations across entire columns.

00:00:22.107 --> 00:00:24.952
This is called vectorized work.

00:00:24.952 --> 00:00:32.959
Instead of writing a Python loop for every row, we describe the calculation once and Pandas applies it to the column.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:36.217
Derived columns are common in analytics.

00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:43.758
Examples include profit margin, customer age group, days since purchase, risk category, or percentage change.

00:00:43.758 --> 00:00:50.567
The key question is whether the new feature helps answer the analytical question.
